introduction.tex-21","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:eb842553439be13607766478bfc91123edc613c183f52424fb7cb2736e302565","file":"preprints/Integrability-of-split-tangent-bundles-on-rationally-connected-manifolds-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"25f61764ef8ea451f985aa00e9942ac6ab30157958710771c0f7749b40fac57b","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Integrability-of-split-tangent-bundles-on-rationally-connected-manifolds-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:eb842553439be13607766478bfc91123edc613c183f52424fb7cb2736e302565","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Integrability-of-split-tangent-bundles-on-rationally-connected-manifolds-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label[theorem]{thm:main}\nLet \\(X\\) be a smooth connected projective complex manifold of dimension\nat least two. Suppose that two general points of \\(X\\) lie on the image\nof a morphism \\(\\PP^1\\to X\\). For every specified holomorphic decomposition\n\\[\nT_X=E_1\\oplus E_2\n\\]\ninto subbundles of positive rank, both \\(E_1\\) and \\(E_2\\) are integrable."}
